vibeos (1:0.1.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Browser: a page whose process ended, because it crashed or because
    the phone ran out of memory, shows "This page stopped working" (or
    "used too much memory") with a Reload button, in place of an empty
    grey view. The address typed is looked up while it is typed, so the
    page starts loading sooner (never in incognito).
  * The charging line on the lock screen and the always-on display comes
    from the power that flows into the battery, as Android has it: under
    5 W "Charging slowly", from 5 W "Charging", from 12 W "Fast charging"
    and from 20 W "Super fast charging", whatever the charger offers. A
    computer's port, or a charger that only just keeps up with the screen,
    now reads "Charging slowly". "Not charging" is said only when the
    battery says so (too warm, or a charge limit).
  * Tablets without a vibration motor (the Xiaomi Pad 5, the Galaxy Tab
    S5e Wi-Fi) click softly under the keyboard's keys and sound each step
    of the volume, as Android does; phones keep their haptics. Settings ›
    Sound and vibration › System sounds has Keyboard sounds and Volume
    change sound, on by default where there is no motor. Both stay silent
    during a call, in Vibrate and Mute, and while the sound is muted.
  * A tablet's cover locks it and puts the screen to sleep when it
    closes, as the power key does, and wakes it to the lock screen when
    it opens, as Android has it (the Xiaomi Pad 5's and the Galaxy Tab
    S5e's). A closed cover no longer asks for a suspend.
  * POCO X3 NFC: a call in an app (a SIP or a video call app) starts on
    the earpiece, as on Android, and its Speaker button moves it to
    the loudspeaker. The ringtone, the dial pad's tones, Vibe and Dictate
    stay on the loudspeaker, and the user's own choice of output is kept.

