vibeos (1:0.1.4.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Built against evolution-data-server 3.62, which is in sid: Contacts,
    Phone, Messages, Calendar and Vibe no longer load EDS 3.56's
    libedataserver beside 3.62's, and 0.1.4's hold of EDS can be lifted.
    The build requires EDS 3.62 now. vCards are written and read through
    3.62's API (e_vcard_convert_to_string, e_vcard_get_attributes_by_name),
    which replaced the calls 3.56 had.
  * Agent is called Vibe where the user sees it: the launcher and the app
    list (a search for Agent still finds it), its window, its settings,
    Settings' Gestures and the package's description. The ids stay
    (vibeos.Agent, vibeos.Dictate, power-hold-agent).
  * Vibe: a power key hold listens on after the key is let go, until the
    speaker pauses, as Android's assistant does after its long press; a
    hold the shell gives up for the power menu sends nothing.
  * Shell: power and volume up open the power menu when pressed as a hand
    does, either key first and held.
  * Shell: a notification's icon is its app's logo in the status bar, on
    the lock screen and on the always-on display, not a white square.
  * Shell: a fullscreen app keeps clear of the camera hole, as on Android.
  * Shell: "Wireless charging" on a charging pad.
  * Shell: vibeos.Shell has the screen's Brightness and ConfirmOwner, the
    owner's PIN or pattern asked for by an app.
  * Keyboard: one closed under a swipe goes, and Back or a touch takes away
    one left on the screen. Console keeps its size and the keys slide in
    over it (vibeos.Shell keyboard-slide-apps, or X-Vibeos-Keyboard=slide
    in an app's desktop file).
  * Video: full screen, by a button beside the menu (f and F11 too), and by
    turning the screen sideways; full screen, a film shot the way the screen
    is turned is cropped to fill it, and one shot the other way stays
    whole.
  * Video: a tap on a control's button no longer hides the controls.
  * Shell: desktop files are read through GioUnix, so GJS no longer warns
    that Gio.DesktopAppInfo has moved.
  * Vibe: the call announcer's autostart entry leaves out
    X-GNOME-Autostart-Phase, which gnome-session warned about at login.
  * Navi: the package's changelog entry is wrapped at 80 columns.
  * Navi: a release's package requires that release's libvibeos, libspongy
    and libtonal at exactly its version, as every other package does; 0.1.4's
    took any since 0.1.3.
  * Terminal, a new app (vibeos-terminal, vibeos.Terminal), takes Console's
    place: GNOME's terminal widget (VTE) made for the touchscreen. A tap
    brings the keyboard over the window with a row of Esc, Tab, Ctrl, Alt
    and the arrows on it (Ctrl and Alt sticky, as Termux's); a long press
    selects with handles and a Copy and Paste toolbar; one finger or two
    scroll and fling, as a mouse wheel would in less, vim or htop; a pinch
    zooms the text. The vibeos metapackage recommends it, the default home
    has it in Console's dock slot, and the launcher shows it instead of
    Console and puts it in Console's places on a home already set up.
    Console stays installed where it was.
  * Video: full screen plays under the camera hole, the hole inside the
    picture, instead of beside a black bar. Settings (in the menu) has Black
    bar at the camera to bring the bar back, live while a film plays. The
    shell keeps the other apps clear of the hole; vibeos.Shell's
    cutout-extend-apps lists the apps that go under it.

